{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaXPCyQMaa13pFoAsmXV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I replaced the `sorry` in `take_append_drop` (Main.lean:11-17) with an induction proof, and `lean Main.lean` now exits with code 0 and no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem take_append_drop (n : Nat) (xs : List α) : myTake n xs ++ myDrop n xs = xs := by\n  induction n generalizing xs with\n  | zero => simp [myTake, myDrop]\n  | succ n ih =>\n    cases xs with\n    | nil => simp [myTake, myDrop]\n    | cons x xs => simp [myTake, myDrop, ih]\n```\n\nThe proof is by induction on `n`, generalizing `xs`:\n- **Zero:** `myTake 0 xs = []` and `myDrop 0 xs = xs`, so the left side is `[] ++ xs = xs`.\n- **Successor, empty list:** both `myTake` and `myDrop` return `[]`, so the goal is `[] ++ [] = []`.\n- **Successor, cons:** the goal reduces to `x :: (myTake n xs ++ myDrop n xs) = x :: xs`, which the induction hypothesis closes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":933,"cache_read_input_tokens":8764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":933},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5888fad4-216a-4df0-b9cf-aa946e127619","uuid":"6754f16d-7983-49c3-b90a-4a8e3137f969","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:07:56.701Z","request_id":"req_011CgaXPCfoBFhF4y5SyMned"}
